  "priorExpiration": "2018-12-10",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Nuh 305.05 Supervision.\n\n(a) The acting administrator shall be supervised by a licensed administrator who is in good standing with the board and has at least 5 years’ experience operating a licensed nursing home.\n\n(b) Any licensed administrator about to become a supervisor of an acting administrator shall notify the OPLC of their intent.\n\n(c) No licensed administrator shall be permitted to supervise more than one acting administrator at a time.\n\n(d) The licensed administrator supervising an acting administrator shall provide at least 8 hours per week of direct onsite supervision of the acting administrator.\n\n(e) The licensed administrator supervising the acting administrator shall be responsible for all aspects of the facility’s operation.\n\nSource. #1393, eff 7-1-79; ss by #2224, eff 1-1-83; ss by #2922, eff 12-10-84, EXPIRED: 12-10-90\n\nNew. #5097, eff 3-18-91; ss by #5326, eff 2-13-92; rsvd by #5524, eff 12-8-92, EXPIRED: 12-8-98\n\nNew. #7663, eff 3-19-02, EXPIRED: 3-19-10\n\nNew. #9830-A, eff 12-10-10, EXPIRED: 12-10-18\n\nNew. #12690, eff 12-19-18; ss by #13935, eff 6-22-24; ss by #14145, eff 2-8-25",
